WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.369 --> 00:00:02.419
- To be loved for one generation,

00:00:02.419 --> 00:00:04.116
remembered for two generations,

00:00:04.116 --> 00:00:05.367
and forgotten after that.

00:00:05.367 --> 00:00:07.412
The best thing that ever happened to me is

00:00:07.412 --> 00:00:08.559
I hit rock bottom.

00:00:08.559 --> 00:00:10.443
By far the best thing
that ever happened to me

00:00:10.443 --> 00:00:11.352
is hitting rock bottom.

00:00:11.352 --> 00:00:13.052
Why can't you be

00:00:13.052 --> 00:00:15.713
somebody that can do
something in your business

00:00:15.713 --> 00:00:17.026
that's never been done before?

00:00:17.026 --> 00:00:17.859
Why not you?

00:00:17.859 --> 00:00:18.884
Answer it.

00:00:18.884 --> 00:00:21.821
- He's an american entrepreneur
and financial advisor.

00:00:21.821 --> 00:00:24.266
He speaks on a range of
topics including leadership

00:00:24.266 --> 00:00:26.311
and how to become an entrepreneur.

00:00:26.311 --> 00:00:27.701
He's published two books,

00:00:27.701 --> 00:00:30.282
The 25 Laws of Doing the Impossible

00:00:30.282 --> 00:00:32.039
and The Next Perfect Storm.

00:00:32.039 --> 00:00:33.187
He's Patrick Bet-David,

00:00:33.187 --> 00:00:35.807
and here is my take on his
top 10 rules for success.

00:00:35.807 --> 00:00:37.462
Rule number 10 is my personal favorite,

00:00:37.462 --> 00:00:38.518
and make sure to stick around

00:00:38.518 --> 00:00:41.259
all the way to the end for
a special bonus message.

00:00:41.259 --> 00:00:42.756
And, as always, if Patrick says something

00:00:42.756 --> 00:00:44.491
that really, really resonates with you,

00:00:44.491 --> 00:00:45.934
please leave it in the comments below

00:00:45.934 --> 00:00:46.906
and put quotes around it

00:00:46.906 --> 00:00:49.002
so other people can be inspired as well.

00:00:49.002 --> 00:00:50.090
Enjoy.

00:00:50.090 --> 00:00:53.180
(whooshing)

00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:55.847
(uptempo music)

00:01:02.942 --> 00:01:07.188
- Man, what happened to Pops
when he started a business?

00:01:07.188 --> 00:01:08.489
He failed.

00:01:08.489 --> 00:01:10.078
What happened to Mom and Dad?

00:01:10.078 --> 00:01:11.549
They got a divorce.

00:01:11.549 --> 00:01:12.992
What happened to us?

00:01:12.992 --> 00:01:15.267
We lived six different places.

00:01:15.267 --> 00:01:16.437
Was it fun?

00:01:16.437 --> 00:01:17.978
Hell no, it wasn't fun.

00:01:17.978 --> 00:01:19.656
What happened in high school to you?

00:01:19.656 --> 00:01:21.090
Did you play baseball?

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:22.663
Did you play high school basketball?

00:01:22.663 --> 00:01:24.056
Did you get picked up for football?

00:01:24.056 --> 00:01:25.344
Did you date the girl you liked?

00:01:25.344 --> 00:01:26.413
What was your GPA?

00:01:26.413 --> 00:01:27.876
Who were you in high school?

00:01:27.876 --> 00:01:29.542
Who were you afterwards?

00:01:29.542 --> 00:01:32.598
What makes you think you're
going to make it in life?

00:01:32.598 --> 00:01:35.352
You got to stop selling
this stuff to this guy, man.

00:01:35.352 --> 00:01:37.819
Stop it, it's getting old.

00:01:37.819 --> 00:01:40.177
Go get that job that you let go of,

00:01:40.177 --> 00:01:42.179
paying you 12 bucks an hour,

00:01:42.179 --> 00:01:43.912
and part-time get a degree.

00:01:43.912 --> 00:01:46.028
Stop taking these damn risks.

00:01:46.028 --> 00:01:48.525
We're not meant to do
something big with our lives,

00:01:48.525 --> 00:01:49.775
simple as that.

00:01:51.290 --> 00:01:52.457
- Are we done?

00:01:55.130 --> 00:01:57.578
- I'm done, I'm good.

00:01:57.578 --> 00:01:58.661
- Okay, good.

00:02:01.327 --> 00:02:03.378
Pat, I want you to know, this voice

00:02:03.378 --> 00:02:04.881
is never going away.

00:02:04.881 --> 00:02:06.723
This voice is always going to be there.

00:02:06.723 --> 00:02:09.129
No matter how much money
you're going to make,

00:02:09.129 --> 00:02:11.098
it's always going to be there.

00:02:11.098 --> 00:02:12.310
The great thing about it is, though,

00:02:12.310 --> 00:02:14.676
every morning you wake
up, you have a choice

00:02:14.676 --> 00:02:16.524
on which voice to listen to.

00:02:16.524 --> 00:02:17.561
But I want you to think about

00:02:17.561 --> 00:02:20.295
a completely different thing right now.

00:02:20.295 --> 00:02:21.909
Let's just say you do nothing.

00:02:21.909 --> 00:02:23.607
Let's just say you buy into your fears.

00:02:23.607 --> 00:02:24.440
Let's just say you buy into

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:26.346
every single thing you're worried about.

00:02:26.346 --> 00:02:27.800
Let's just say you
don't make any decisions

00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:28.938
to go after your dreams.

00:02:28.938 --> 00:02:30.271
Fast forward 10 years from now,

00:02:30.271 --> 00:02:33.521
20 years from now, 30 years
from now, 40 years from now.

00:02:33.521 --> 00:02:35.288
Let's just say your
funeral's around the corner.

00:02:35.288 --> 00:02:37.033
You have 50 people
there, 100 people there,

00:02:37.033 --> 00:02:39.016
maybe 200 people show up.

00:02:39.016 --> 00:02:41.858
These are your friends, family,
and people that love you.

00:02:41.858 --> 00:02:43.944
So you'll be loved for one generation,

00:02:43.944 --> 00:02:45.680
remembered for two generations,

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:47.181
and forgotten after that.

00:02:47.181 --> 00:02:49.125
Is that truly the life you want to live?

00:02:49.125 --> 00:02:51.421
Is that really what you want to do?

00:02:51.421 --> 00:02:53.981
I don't know if that's the
life you really want to live.

00:02:53.981 --> 00:02:55.270
You see, what I've noticed is,

00:02:55.270 --> 00:02:56.428
no matter what you ever do,

00:02:56.428 --> 00:02:58.227
you'll have a lot of lonely times.

00:02:58.227 --> 00:03:00.491
You can lie to your family,
you can lie to your friends,

00:03:00.491 --> 00:03:02.474
you can fool the world into realizing that

00:03:02.474 --> 00:03:03.713
why you didn't win was because of

00:03:03.713 --> 00:03:05.774
some challenge that you had to face.

00:03:05.774 --> 00:03:08.720
But there's one person
you can never lie to,

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:10.398
and that is the man in the mirror.

00:03:10.398 --> 00:03:13.506
You can never lie to the
man in the mirror, never.

00:03:13.506 --> 00:03:15.355
For the rest of your life,
the man in the mirror

00:03:15.355 --> 00:03:17.934
is going to look back at you and say,

00:03:17.934 --> 00:03:20.658
"You did not choose to
go after your dreams."

00:03:20.658 --> 00:03:22.661
And you have to be okay with that.

00:03:22.661 --> 00:03:25.322
Now, what I would like
to encourage you to do is

00:03:25.322 --> 00:03:27.191
to make the right choice.

00:03:27.191 --> 00:03:28.553
I encourage you to face your fears

00:03:28.553 --> 00:03:30.573
and pursue your dreams.

00:03:30.573 --> 00:03:32.726
Go pursue the dreams that
matter the most to you.

00:03:32.726 --> 00:03:34.941
You only got one shot at this thing here,

00:03:34.941 --> 00:03:36.680
and if it works out, man,

00:03:36.680 --> 00:03:38.892
it's going to feel so good for you.

00:03:38.892 --> 00:03:40.935
And if it doesn't, at
least you had the courage

00:03:40.935 --> 00:03:43.007
to make that decision.

00:03:43.007 --> 00:03:45.741
I hope you make the right choice.

00:03:45.741 --> 00:03:47.244
I trust you will.

00:03:47.244 --> 00:03:48.928
Let me tell you one thing that, you know,

00:03:48.928 --> 00:03:52.312
most millionaires master
is reading people.

00:03:52.312 --> 00:03:53.897
Reading people, and I'll tell you

00:03:53.897 --> 00:03:56.897
what I mean by reading people, okay?

00:03:58.213 --> 00:04:00.131
The reason why reading people,

00:04:00.131 --> 00:04:02.876
millionaires end up generally
become good at reading people

00:04:02.876 --> 00:04:04.198
is because they've been ripped off,

00:04:04.198 --> 00:04:07.570
back-stabbed, lied to,
cheated so many times

00:04:07.570 --> 00:04:09.094
that there are a lot of signals

00:04:09.094 --> 00:04:11.593
that they see a trend of
saying this person's like that,

00:04:11.593 --> 00:04:13.239
reminds me of this person.

00:04:13.239 --> 00:04:14.377
You got to learn how to read people,

00:04:14.377 --> 00:04:15.605
you got to learn how to read a customer,

00:04:15.605 --> 00:04:17.573
you got to learn how to read an employee,

00:04:17.573 --> 00:04:19.860
you got to learn how to read

00:04:19.860 --> 00:04:22.219
someone who is absolutely full of it.

00:04:22.219 --> 00:04:24.117
Sometimes I get surprised

00:04:24.117 --> 00:04:26.647
how some people who are pretty successful,

00:04:26.647 --> 00:04:29.004
they're making $100,
$200, $300,000 a year,

00:04:29.004 --> 00:04:31.929
how easily they fall for the trap of

00:04:31.929 --> 00:04:33.089
somebody who's full of it.

00:04:33.089 --> 00:04:35.240
Like, how do you not read
that sometimes, right?

00:04:35.240 --> 00:04:37.004
You got to learn how to read it,

00:04:37.004 --> 00:04:41.169
and a certain level of paranoia
when you're reading people.

00:04:41.169 --> 00:04:44.054
And then also, when I'm
saying reading people,

00:04:44.054 --> 00:04:45.767
it's not just on a negative side.

00:04:45.767 --> 00:04:48.227
Reading people on someone that's truly,

00:04:48.227 --> 00:04:49.355
you did something wrong

00:04:49.355 --> 00:04:51.153
and you need to go out there
and do something about it.

00:04:51.153 --> 00:04:52.210
You need to read people that need

00:04:52.210 --> 00:04:55.319
you to make a right effort
to take care of them.

00:04:55.319 --> 00:04:57.473
You don't make the right effort to

00:04:57.473 --> 00:04:59.313
treat them in a way that
they need to be treated.

00:04:59.313 --> 00:05:00.550
That's also reading people.

00:05:00.550 --> 00:05:03.507
Another one is when I
say reading people is

00:05:03.507 --> 00:05:07.388
being able to think what a
customer is going to need now,

00:05:07.388 --> 00:05:08.871
and what a customer is going
to need a year from now,

00:05:08.871 --> 00:05:10.729
three years from now, five years from now,

00:05:10.729 --> 00:05:11.562
and reading them.

00:05:11.562 --> 00:05:13.236
Being able to read a person

00:05:13.236 --> 00:05:16.258
that starts with your
company at an early stage,

00:05:16.258 --> 00:05:17.639
and what were they thinking about

00:05:17.639 --> 00:05:18.847
when they were at your level.

00:05:18.847 --> 00:05:20.513
At a new level, you're
not speaking to them

00:05:20.513 --> 00:05:21.346
from your level.

00:05:21.346 --> 00:05:24.211
Millionaires, they got
to learn how to read

00:05:24.211 --> 00:05:26.658
somebody at that level
and give them the belief

00:05:26.658 --> 00:05:28.051
that they need at that level,

00:05:28.051 --> 00:05:30.591
versus somebody that's
been around a little longer

00:05:30.591 --> 00:05:33.415
that needs to kind of man up, or woman up,

00:05:33.415 --> 00:05:35.191
or mature as an entrepreneur,
and they're not,

00:05:35.191 --> 00:05:37.162
they're just treating this as a

00:05:37.162 --> 00:05:38.373
lolligagging with the industry,

00:05:38.373 --> 00:05:39.470
and that's a completely
different conversation

00:05:39.470 --> 00:05:40.303
with that person.

00:05:40.303 --> 00:05:41.136
Say, "Grow up already.

00:05:41.136 --> 00:05:42.334
"You've been in this thing
for five, 10, 15 years,

00:05:42.334 --> 00:05:43.167
"what's next?

00:05:43.167 --> 00:05:44.742
"You're going to be like
this your entire life?"

00:05:44.742 --> 00:05:48.921
So, reading to know when,
where, who, what, when.

00:05:48.921 --> 00:05:50.945
They eventually become very
good at reading people.

00:05:50.945 --> 00:05:52.917
I like shining shoes.

00:05:52.917 --> 00:05:54.682
I like ironing clothes.

00:05:54.682 --> 00:05:56.664
I like doing those types of things.

00:05:56.664 --> 00:05:59.174
And I remember one time,
one of my mentors said,

00:05:59.174 --> 00:06:01.073
"Do you want to make $10 an hour?"

00:06:01.073 --> 00:06:01.906
I said no.

00:06:01.906 --> 00:06:03.978
"Then why do you keep
doing $10 an hour jobs?"

00:06:03.978 --> 00:06:04.811
I said, "What do you mean?"

00:06:04.811 --> 00:06:05.656
He says, "You keep shining shoes,

00:06:05.656 --> 00:06:08.224
"you keep doing this, you keep
liking those types of things,

00:06:08.224 --> 00:06:09.597
"you got to get somebody
else to help you out."

00:06:09.597 --> 00:06:10.796
So what happened?

00:06:10.796 --> 00:06:14.522
I went 100% dry cleaners, even
when I couldn't afford it.

00:06:14.522 --> 00:06:15.518
I was broke.

00:06:15.518 --> 00:06:17.866
I went 100% dry cleaners.

00:06:17.866 --> 00:06:20.760
I went 100% somebody else
helping my shine my shoes,

00:06:20.760 --> 00:06:22.589
and I gave money to a business.

00:06:22.589 --> 00:06:25.188
I got an assistant to
do my paperwork for me,

00:06:25.188 --> 00:06:26.307
to do the filing for me,

00:06:26.307 --> 00:06:28.277
to do all of those things for me,

00:06:28.277 --> 00:06:31.021
to drop my car off at Jiffy
Lube to get an oil change,

00:06:31.021 --> 00:06:32.240
to get a car wash.

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:34.446
Literally all of those activities

00:06:34.446 --> 00:06:35.907
were done by somebody else,

00:06:35.907 --> 00:06:37.746
and it became a match-up system to me.

00:06:37.746 --> 00:06:39.940
I had somebody do those things for me,

00:06:39.940 --> 00:06:41.922
were allowing me to do the other things,

00:06:41.922 --> 00:06:44.368
even housecleaning, it
was somebody else doing it

00:06:44.368 --> 00:06:45.498
where it's not me doing it.

00:06:45.498 --> 00:06:46.778
Now, why is that important to do?

00:06:46.778 --> 00:06:49.399
You got to get an assistant
so you can leverage your time.

00:06:49.399 --> 00:06:51.654
Do not let $10 an hour job

00:06:51.654 --> 00:06:53.834
get you out of business,
where you end up going back

00:06:53.834 --> 00:06:56.175
and getting a job that
pays you only $10 an hour.

00:06:56.175 --> 00:06:57.931
Focus on what grows your business.

00:06:57.931 --> 00:07:00.584
I got a call from one of my friends

00:07:00.584 --> 00:07:02.688
from many, many, many years ago,

00:07:02.688 --> 00:07:05.207
growing up and he said, you know,

00:07:05.207 --> 00:07:07.057
he's been trying to get
into a relationship,

00:07:07.057 --> 00:07:09.117
and he says, "Pat," he's an entrepreneur,

00:07:09.117 --> 00:07:11.241
he says, "Pat, I'm dating this girl,

00:07:11.241 --> 00:07:12.969
"and I'm at a point right now

00:07:12.969 --> 00:07:14.229
"where I feel like I need to settle down.

00:07:14.229 --> 00:07:15.468
"I'm in my mid-30s."

00:07:15.468 --> 00:07:16.675
I said, "Okay."

00:07:16.675 --> 00:07:19.296
He says, "But she told me this."

00:07:19.296 --> 00:07:20.129
I said, "What'd she tell you?"

00:07:20.129 --> 00:07:22.394
She says, "It's either me or the business,

00:07:22.394 --> 00:07:23.432
"because she can't stand the fact

00:07:23.432 --> 00:07:24.794
"that I'm working the way that I am

00:07:24.794 --> 00:07:26.631
"and I'm running a business."

00:07:26.631 --> 00:07:27.789
And I said, "What's your answer?"

00:07:27.789 --> 00:07:28.622
He says, "Well, I don't know.

00:07:28.622 --> 00:07:29.455
"What do you think I should do?"

00:07:29.455 --> 00:07:31.803
I said, "Well, I'm not going
to give you my advice."

00:07:31.803 --> 00:07:35.723
I said, "What's, how
are you wired yourself?"

00:07:35.723 --> 00:07:37.980
He says, "Pat, I don't
think I can really do this."

00:07:37.980 --> 00:07:39.277
I said, "Why do you think?"

00:07:39.277 --> 00:07:42.185
He says, "Because you're
asking me to change myself."

00:07:42.185 --> 00:07:44.573
You see, when somebody says,

00:07:44.573 --> 00:07:46.655
"It's either me or the business,"

00:07:46.655 --> 00:07:49.227
let me explain to you how
an entrepreneur sees that,

00:07:49.227 --> 00:07:51.624
so maybe it'll help understand.

00:07:51.624 --> 00:07:56.387
The entrepreneur says,
"It's either your arm or me,

00:07:56.387 --> 00:07:58.532
"what's more important?"

00:07:58.532 --> 00:08:00.918
I love you, but I'm not
going to cut my arm off.

00:08:00.918 --> 00:08:02.492
You're telling me to be a
whole different human being

00:08:02.492 --> 00:08:03.977
to be with you.

00:08:03.977 --> 00:08:06.035
We're not living in Biblical times.

00:08:06.035 --> 00:08:08.192
I'm not going to cut my arm off for you.

00:08:08.192 --> 00:08:09.239
If you want me, this is me.

00:08:09.239 --> 00:08:10.072
This is how I come.

00:08:10.072 --> 00:08:11.279
Do you like it?

00:08:11.279 --> 00:08:13.567
You don't like it, go find somebody else.

00:08:13.567 --> 00:08:15.506
But this is how I'm wired.

00:08:15.506 --> 00:08:18.046
I've been like this for 22 years.

00:08:18.046 --> 00:08:19.683
I've been like this for 38 years.

00:08:19.683 --> 00:08:20.617
It doesn't mean I'm not going to change

00:08:20.617 --> 00:08:21.999
and improve myself with maturity.

00:08:21.999 --> 00:08:24.730
I am, but I'm an entrepreneur.

00:08:24.730 --> 00:08:27.606
I'm in the hunt, I'm going after it.

00:08:27.606 --> 00:08:28.439
I'm going to build something

00:08:28.439 --> 00:08:30.053
special and significant for my life,

00:08:30.053 --> 00:08:31.626
and I want to build it with you,

00:08:31.626 --> 00:08:33.649
but not if you're trying to change me.

00:08:33.649 --> 00:08:36.207
So, on the other side, somebody may say,

00:08:36.207 --> 00:08:37.469
"Well, they spend more
time with the business.

00:08:37.469 --> 00:08:39.451
"They love the business
more than they love me."

00:08:39.451 --> 00:08:41.284
No, it's how they are.

00:08:42.151 --> 00:08:44.814
It's how they are, it's how they're wired.

00:08:44.814 --> 00:08:46.231
If somebody says,

00:08:48.483 --> 00:08:50.381
"Babe, I'm pregnant,

00:08:50.381 --> 00:08:51.214
"what do you want me to do?"

00:08:51.214 --> 00:08:52.454
When you're pregnant, you go through this.

00:08:52.454 --> 00:08:55.217
A man may feel like, "But
what's more important to you,

00:08:55.217 --> 00:08:56.062
"the baby or me?"

00:08:56.062 --> 00:08:57.951
What are you talking about?

00:08:57.951 --> 00:08:59.768
This is something that we don't understand

00:08:59.768 --> 00:09:00.762
when a first pregnancy.

00:09:00.762 --> 00:09:02.327
We're on our third one now,

00:09:02.327 --> 00:09:04.927
so now I get an understanding of it.

00:09:04.927 --> 00:09:07.123
It's like, "Who's more
important, me or the baby?

00:09:07.123 --> 00:09:08.690
"I'm your husband."

00:09:08.690 --> 00:09:10.906
That's an ultimatum.

00:09:10.906 --> 00:09:13.444
You don't put a mother
in a position like that.

00:09:13.444 --> 00:09:15.111
You don't put an entrepreneur
in a position to say

00:09:15.111 --> 00:09:16.716
it's the business or me.

00:09:16.716 --> 00:09:18.966
They'll typically take them

00:09:19.805 --> 00:09:21.866
as who they are for a human being.

00:09:21.866 --> 00:09:23.381
'Cause the last thing you
want is to date somebody,

00:09:23.381 --> 00:09:26.936
and then 10, 20 years
later they have resentment.

00:09:26.936 --> 00:09:29.049
Then it can lead to worse things.

00:09:29.049 --> 00:09:32.198
You had somebody that decided
to change their own DNA

00:09:32.198 --> 00:09:35.115
to be with you, all because of you.

00:09:36.332 --> 00:09:38.395
You have a delayed time bomb

00:09:38.395 --> 00:09:40.044
of someone that could eventually become

00:09:40.044 --> 00:09:42.569
your biggest enemy in your life,

00:09:42.569 --> 00:09:44.296
because you tried to change them.

00:09:44.296 --> 00:09:46.064
I don't recommend that.

00:09:46.064 --> 00:09:47.201
One of the best recommendations I got

00:09:47.201 --> 00:09:48.034
before I got married,

00:09:48.034 --> 00:09:49.936
I was dating a girl at one point,

00:09:49.936 --> 00:09:52.313
and I went to one of my
mentors, one of my pastors,

00:09:52.313 --> 00:09:55.733
and I said, "Hey, this
is what I'm experiencing,

00:09:55.733 --> 00:09:57.116
"what do you think?"

00:09:57.116 --> 00:09:57.961
He said, "Does it bother you?"

00:09:57.961 --> 00:09:59.676
I said, "A lot."

00:09:59.676 --> 00:10:01.555
He said, "Can you deal without it?"

00:10:01.555 --> 00:10:05.011
I said, "No, I cannot,
I can't deal with this."

00:10:05.011 --> 00:10:08.108
And he said, "It's just going to get more,

00:10:08.108 --> 00:10:09.507
"so if you can't deal with it now,

00:10:09.507 --> 00:10:11.664
"don't think it's going to disappear."

00:10:11.664 --> 00:10:13.240
And I have to make that
decision and move on.

00:10:13.240 --> 00:10:14.792
It wasn't easy, it was
very difficult because,

00:10:14.792 --> 00:10:16.803
you know, I really cared
for this human being,

00:10:16.803 --> 00:10:18.328
but I have to move on.

00:10:18.328 --> 00:10:22.931
So, if somebody's really
trying to change somebody,

00:10:22.931 --> 00:10:24.929
and you're an entrepreneur,

00:10:24.929 --> 00:10:26.506
if the person does change,

00:10:26.506 --> 00:10:27.828
it's just a matter of time

00:10:27.828 --> 00:10:29.351
'til the person goes back to

00:10:29.351 --> 00:10:31.036
being true to who they are.

00:10:31.036 --> 00:10:32.289
You're going to be true
back to who you are.

00:10:32.289 --> 00:10:34.564
The entrepreneur, the real entrepreneur,

00:10:34.564 --> 00:10:36.857
is going to go back
being true to themselves.

00:10:36.857 --> 00:10:39.592
I was a young kid, just a knucklehead

00:10:39.592 --> 00:10:41.423
who thought he knew everything.

00:10:41.423 --> 00:10:44.072
You know, 21 years old, I
would've been so annoyed

00:10:44.072 --> 00:10:45.628
coaching myself at that time,

00:10:45.628 --> 00:10:47.558
'cause I thought I knew everything.

00:10:47.558 --> 00:10:49.895
And then the best thing
that ever happened to me,

00:10:49.895 --> 00:10:51.772
the best thing that ever happened to me is

00:10:51.772 --> 00:10:53.051
I hit rock bottom.

00:10:53.051 --> 00:10:54.881
By far the best thing
that ever happened to me

00:10:54.881 --> 00:10:55.714
is hitting rock bottom.

00:10:55.714 --> 00:10:58.419
I think, for men, I have two boys,

00:10:58.419 --> 00:11:00.390
and I'm going to be in pain when I witness

00:11:00.390 --> 00:11:02.178
these guys go through this,

00:11:02.178 --> 00:11:04.242
but I think the best thing
that can happen to a man

00:11:04.242 --> 00:11:06.871
is a heartbreak, a very strong heartbreak,

00:11:06.871 --> 00:11:10.073
and a very big failure
early on in business.

00:11:10.073 --> 00:11:11.942
And it happened to me early on in life,

00:11:11.942 --> 00:11:13.393
both heartbreak and business.

00:11:13.393 --> 00:11:16.269
It happened early on because
I thought I knew it all,

00:11:16.269 --> 00:11:17.773
and it was a slap in the face to say,

00:11:17.773 --> 00:11:19.326
if Socrates says, "The only thing I know

00:11:19.326 --> 00:11:20.963
"is that I know nothing."

00:11:20.963 --> 00:11:22.821
If the greatest minds, on their deathbed,

00:11:22.821 --> 00:11:23.857
are saying things like that,

00:11:23.857 --> 00:11:25.970
what makes you and I
think we know everything?

00:11:25.970 --> 00:11:28.135
Quite frankly, everything
I'm saying on Valuetainment

00:11:28.135 --> 00:11:29.383
may be inaccurate.

00:11:29.383 --> 00:11:31.284
Every single thing I'm
saying on Valuetainment,

00:11:31.284 --> 00:11:33.345
you may come back and my
opinions may be wrong.

00:11:33.345 --> 00:11:34.635
It's worked for me.

00:11:34.635 --> 00:11:35.876
This is how it's worked for me.

00:11:35.876 --> 00:11:37.258
For me, it's more about
teaching how to think

00:11:37.258 --> 00:11:39.054
than actually what to think.

00:11:39.054 --> 00:11:40.781
I want to get an entrepreneur to learn

00:11:40.781 --> 00:11:42.825
how to think than what to think.

00:11:42.825 --> 00:11:44.511
But we don't know everything.

00:11:44.511 --> 00:11:45.596
We got to learn how to adjust,

00:11:45.596 --> 00:11:46.531
we got to learn how to adapt,

00:11:46.531 --> 00:11:47.477
we got to learn how to get better,

00:11:47.477 --> 00:11:48.859
we got to learn how to improve,

00:11:48.859 --> 00:11:50.534
and so the mindset of
thinking you know it all,

00:11:50.534 --> 00:11:53.166
it's just not a place you want to be,

00:11:53.166 --> 00:11:55.836
'cause it means advancement
doesn't come around the corner,

00:11:55.836 --> 00:11:58.193
and I had the know-it-all
attitude at a young age,

00:11:58.193 --> 00:11:59.505
and it almost cost me.

00:11:59.505 --> 00:12:01.048
There's a benefit to that.

00:12:01.048 --> 00:12:02.945
There's a benefit because you become edgy,

00:12:02.945 --> 00:12:04.605
you push the envelope a little bit,

00:12:04.605 --> 00:12:08.738
but there's also the leveling off to know

00:12:08.738 --> 00:12:10.546
that maybe you don't really know this,

00:12:10.546 --> 00:12:12.741
so let me ask and question
somebody I respect

00:12:12.741 --> 00:12:15.251
to give me proper direction that I trust

00:12:15.251 --> 00:12:18.400
that maybe they can challenge
my position and opinion,

00:12:18.400 --> 00:12:20.096
but it's good that I have the audacity,

00:12:20.096 --> 00:12:22.960
so I like it, the fact
that there's audacity,

00:12:22.960 --> 00:12:24.464
that you're pushing the envelope,

00:12:24.464 --> 00:12:26.292
but there's got to be coachability

00:12:26.292 --> 00:12:30.571
and learnability that you want
to learn and advance as well.

00:12:30.571 --> 00:12:31.798
It doesn't matter who you are,

00:12:31.798 --> 00:12:33.801
everyone's got to have somebody
that they have a mentor

00:12:33.801 --> 00:12:35.415
that's giving them direction with.

00:12:35.415 --> 00:12:37.856
So it was good that I got
out of that pretty quickly.

00:12:37.856 --> 00:12:39.439
Energy and stamina.

00:12:40.428 --> 00:12:43.036
It requires energy and
stamina to retain information.

00:12:43.036 --> 00:12:47.182
So, if your body is
gaining too much weight,

00:12:47.182 --> 00:12:48.909
and you're tired,

00:12:48.909 --> 00:12:51.185
your body doesn't have
the energy and the stamina

00:12:51.185 --> 00:12:53.684
to retain that information.

00:12:53.684 --> 00:12:56.215
To retain information requires your body

00:12:56.215 --> 00:12:58.916
to have the energy to retain it.

00:12:58.916 --> 00:13:00.955
If it doesn't have it, it's
not going to retain it.

00:13:00.955 --> 00:13:02.512
Come on, Pat, you're telling me my weight

00:13:02.512 --> 00:13:03.740
has to do with retaining information?

00:13:03.740 --> 00:13:05.823
Yes it does, yes it does.

00:13:06.718 --> 00:13:10.498
'Cause retaining information
requires an effort,

00:13:10.498 --> 00:13:12.599
and any time you need to take
an effort to do anything,

00:13:12.599 --> 00:13:14.244
it's going to deplete what?

00:13:14.244 --> 00:13:15.598
Energy.

00:13:15.598 --> 00:13:18.400
And if you don't have
the energy in your mind,

00:13:18.400 --> 00:13:21.567
it just says I don't have any interest

00:13:22.566 --> 00:13:25.460
to want to retain this
information 'cause I'm tired,

00:13:25.460 --> 00:13:28.134
and I don't have stamina,
and my energy's low.

00:13:28.134 --> 00:13:31.312
That's why energy's a
very, very important gain,

00:13:31.312 --> 00:13:32.856
and it's not just about money.

00:13:32.856 --> 00:13:34.522
Energy is not just about looks,

00:13:34.522 --> 00:13:38.008
and looking pretty, and exercising
'cause I want to look good.

00:13:38.008 --> 00:13:39.552
Exercise when we're younger was for

00:13:39.552 --> 00:13:40.982
a whole different purpose.

00:13:40.982 --> 00:13:43.096
When you're married with kids
and later on you're an adult,

00:13:43.096 --> 00:13:44.733
you're exercising for a
whole different reason.

00:13:44.733 --> 00:13:46.683
Focus, energy, and stamina.

00:13:46.683 --> 00:13:47.983
Sharper mind.

00:13:47.983 --> 00:13:49.852
Selling is something you'll always do

00:13:49.852 --> 00:13:50.685
the rest of your life.

00:13:50.685 --> 00:13:51.600
Most people don't like selling.

00:13:51.600 --> 00:13:53.704
Some people like to kind of make it nicer,

00:13:53.704 --> 00:13:54.720
and some will use a better word

00:13:54.720 --> 00:13:56.386
and say communication or this.

00:13:56.386 --> 00:13:57.219
It's sales.

00:13:57.219 --> 00:14:00.011
By the way, those that
just turned off the video

00:14:00.011 --> 00:14:01.930
and don't want to watch
about what selling has to do,

00:14:01.930 --> 00:14:03.782
hey, you want to marry that girl you love?

00:14:03.782 --> 00:14:04.987
You know which one I'm talking about?

00:14:04.987 --> 00:14:07.213
You need to sell her, and her parents,

00:14:07.213 --> 00:14:08.536
and her best friends.

00:14:08.536 --> 00:14:09.753
That's all selling.

00:14:09.753 --> 00:14:11.075
You want to get that promotion?

00:14:11.075 --> 00:14:12.504
Purely selling, baby.

00:14:12.504 --> 00:14:13.929
And those who get that promotion

00:14:13.929 --> 00:14:15.464
sell better than you do.

00:14:15.464 --> 00:14:16.563
That's the way it is.

00:14:16.563 --> 00:14:18.035
They don't sell a car.

00:14:18.035 --> 00:14:19.844
Their job could be human
resources or something,

00:14:19.844 --> 00:14:22.130
but they learn how to sell themselves

00:14:22.130 --> 00:14:23.643
as that position more than you.

00:14:23.643 --> 00:14:24.964
Maybe you ought to learn how to do it.

00:14:24.964 --> 00:14:26.815
It'll benefit you, make
you a lot of money.

00:14:26.815 --> 00:14:30.227
Picasso once said, "Good artists copy,

00:14:30.227 --> 00:14:32.423
"great artists steal."

00:14:32.423 --> 00:14:35.288
This is one of Steve
Jobs's favorite quotes.

00:14:35.288 --> 00:14:39.247
And Steve Jobs once said, "We
have always been shameless

00:14:39.247 --> 00:14:41.598
"about stealing great ideas."

00:14:41.598 --> 00:14:44.158
So wait a minute, is it
a good or a bad thing

00:14:44.158 --> 00:14:46.706
to steal great ideas, and
being a great copycat?

00:14:46.706 --> 00:14:48.271
'Cause I hear some people say sometimes,

00:14:48.271 --> 00:14:49.833
"You know that guy copied my idea?

00:14:49.833 --> 00:14:52.923
"That was my idea, I came up with this."

00:14:52.923 --> 00:14:56.287
Listen, worry when nobody's
copying what you're doing,

00:14:56.287 --> 00:14:58.386
because no one's paying attention to you.

00:14:58.386 --> 00:15:01.680
It is a very, very, very big compliment

00:15:01.680 --> 00:15:03.040
when somebody copies you.

00:15:03.040 --> 00:15:04.269
Ask the question when you're thinking big,

00:15:04.269 --> 00:15:05.877
why not you?

00:15:05.877 --> 00:15:06.974
And answer it.

00:15:06.974 --> 00:15:08.925
I'm not just doing this
motivational video.

00:15:08.925 --> 00:15:10.080
Why not you?

00:15:10.080 --> 00:15:11.058
Why shouldn't you win?

00:15:11.058 --> 00:15:13.232
No, no, no, forget
motivational, let's get logical.

00:15:13.232 --> 00:15:14.065
Why not you?

00:15:14.065 --> 00:15:15.467
Actually answer that.

00:15:15.467 --> 00:15:17.550
Why can't you be somebody

00:15:19.052 --> 00:15:20.332
that can do something in your business

00:15:20.332 --> 00:15:21.725
that's never been done before?

00:15:21.725 --> 00:15:22.558
Why not you?

00:15:22.558 --> 00:15:23.592
Answer it.

00:15:23.592 --> 00:15:25.025
So give the argument.

00:15:25.025 --> 00:15:28.084
Logically, here's why not me.

00:15:28.084 --> 00:15:29.310
Because I don't work hard enough.

00:15:29.310 --> 00:15:30.319
You can fix that.

00:15:30.319 --> 00:15:32.318
Stop being lazy.

00:15:32.318 --> 00:15:34.574
Well, whatever, but because

00:15:34.574 --> 00:15:35.622
I'm not that good in sales.

00:15:35.622 --> 00:15:37.715
You can learn sales.

00:15:37.715 --> 00:15:41.401
So, okay, because I don't
know much about the product.

00:15:41.401 --> 00:15:42.640
You can learn the product.

00:15:42.640 --> 00:15:43.973
But why not you?

00:15:45.334 --> 00:15:46.907
Because no one in my family's been rich.

00:15:46.907 --> 00:15:47.740
So what?

00:15:47.740 --> 00:15:49.507
No one was rich in Zuckerburg's family

00:15:49.507 --> 00:15:51.021
before he became who he is today,

00:15:51.021 --> 00:15:52.341
and nobody was in Jobs's.

00:15:52.341 --> 00:15:55.758
Jobs's mom even gave him up for adoption.

00:15:56.686 --> 00:15:58.693
So, whatever, but, so why not you?

00:15:58.693 --> 00:16:00.023
Make the argument.

00:16:00.023 --> 00:16:01.193
Why not you?

00:16:01.193 --> 00:16:02.693
Truly get into it.

00:16:03.549 --> 00:16:06.179
Then, give the other argument.

00:16:06.179 --> 00:16:09.178
Why aren't you actually doing this?

00:16:09.178 --> 00:16:11.827
Why shouldn't you be the person?

00:16:11.827 --> 00:16:15.160
And say, I'm a very smart person.

00:16:15.160 --> 00:16:17.029
I love people.

00:16:17.029 --> 00:16:18.736
I actually like to make money,

00:16:18.736 --> 00:16:20.686
to make a difference in the world.

00:16:20.686 --> 00:16:21.519
And you know what?

00:16:21.519 --> 00:16:24.009
I care for people, and I have
some things I want to do.

00:16:24.009 --> 00:16:25.613
If I get money in my
pocket, it'll be good,

00:16:25.613 --> 00:16:26.976
I'll do good with it.

00:16:26.976 --> 00:16:28.874
And I got a big heart, and I am talented,

00:16:28.874 --> 00:16:30.817
and da da da da da, and
I know the right people.

00:16:30.817 --> 00:16:32.900
Boom, that's why not you.

00:16:33.792 --> 00:16:35.838
Make both cases, as if you're an attorney

00:16:35.838 --> 00:16:37.389
representing yourself.

00:16:37.389 --> 00:16:40.911
One, why not you, meaning
you shouldn't be the person,

00:16:40.911 --> 00:16:42.112
and the other, why not you,

00:16:42.112 --> 00:16:43.629
meaning you should be the person.

00:16:43.629 --> 00:16:46.624
Sell both of them, and then
see which argument wins.

00:16:46.624 --> 00:16:49.033
Something tells me the argument
on this side's going to win.

00:16:49.033 --> 00:16:50.557
But make that argument.

00:16:50.557 --> 00:16:51.898
Take a sheet of paper
and make that argument.

00:16:51.898 --> 00:16:53.593
Why not you?

00:16:53.593 --> 00:16:55.299
Question that a little bit.

00:16:55.299 --> 00:16:57.120
Who convinced you you can't do it?

00:16:57.120 --> 00:16:59.726
Who convinced you you can't
be part of a group of people?

00:16:59.726 --> 00:17:02.071
I watch so many guys on YouTube that,

00:17:02.071 --> 00:17:03.960
you know, are, even some of these

00:17:03.960 --> 00:17:05.374
guys are considered experts

00:17:05.374 --> 00:17:07.081
by big magazines and have written

00:17:07.081 --> 00:17:08.390
New York Times bestsellers,

00:17:08.390 --> 00:17:11.216
and they say some shit
like, "Oh, you know,

00:17:11.216 --> 00:17:12.261
"entrepreneurs are born."

00:17:12.261 --> 00:17:14.011
Give me a damn break!

00:17:15.054 --> 00:17:17.960
Entrepreneurship can be taught.

00:17:17.960 --> 00:17:19.657
Entrepreneurship is an inspiration

00:17:19.657 --> 00:17:21.272
that comes from here from some people

00:17:21.272 --> 00:17:23.253
that want to solve a bigger problem.

00:17:23.253 --> 00:17:24.208
What do you mean entrepreneurship

00:17:24.208 --> 00:17:25.723
is something you're born with?

00:17:25.723 --> 00:17:28.588
I completely disagree with that statement.

00:17:28.588 --> 00:17:30.566
Fully disagree with that statement.

00:17:30.566 --> 00:17:32.367
Jumping 48 inches?

00:17:32.367 --> 00:17:33.595
That's God-given ability.

00:17:33.595 --> 00:17:34.602
You can't do that.

00:17:34.602 --> 00:17:37.171
Entrepreneurship, it is a formula.

00:17:37.171 --> 00:17:39.120
If you hang around other
people that think like this,

00:17:39.120 --> 00:17:40.604
and you watch this video,

00:17:40.604 --> 00:17:41.753
and you watch all of Valuetainment

00:17:41.753 --> 00:17:42.910
or some other people that are feeding

00:17:42.910 --> 00:17:44.749
the right type of content to you,

00:17:44.749 --> 00:17:46.049
and the right books you read,

00:17:46.049 --> 00:17:48.844
your imagination won't stop working,

00:17:48.844 --> 00:17:52.177
because the entrepreneur is numbers,

00:17:52.177 --> 00:17:54.432
solving problems, how can
I do it better, faster.

00:17:54.432 --> 00:17:58.026
Why can't you learn the skillsets?

00:17:58.026 --> 00:17:58.859
Why can't you?

00:17:58.859 --> 00:18:00.649
You can, so why not you?

00:18:00.649 --> 00:18:02.769
And don't let anybody convince you

00:18:02.769 --> 00:18:04.712
that people who solve some big problems

00:18:04.712 --> 00:18:07.586
and are big thinkers have to be born

00:18:07.586 --> 00:18:08.552
being big thinkers.

00:18:08.552 --> 00:18:09.765
I'm here to tell you

00:18:09.765 --> 00:18:12.398
you can figure out the
formula to thinking bigger.

00:18:12.398 --> 00:18:14.521
Don't let them convince you
that these elite people.

00:18:14.521 --> 00:18:16.573
Sometimes I sit around my friends,

00:18:16.573 --> 00:18:18.177
who are worth money as well.

00:18:18.177 --> 00:18:19.314
I'm around these guys all the time,

00:18:19.314 --> 00:18:21.124
so now, you know, "Hey, Pat,

00:18:21.124 --> 00:18:21.957
"come run the meeting,

00:18:21.957 --> 00:18:23.625
"we're going to go have some
party with these billionaires,

00:18:23.625 --> 00:18:24.458
"are we're going to go hang out?

00:18:24.458 --> 00:18:26.206
"Okay, great, I'm going
to go with these guys, eh.

00:18:26.206 --> 00:18:28.948
"You know, I was always
special because for--"

00:18:28.948 --> 00:18:31.131
Oh my gosh, stop it already.

00:18:31.131 --> 00:18:32.299
When you almost lost everything

00:18:32.299 --> 00:18:34.036
you did not think you were special.

00:18:34.036 --> 00:18:35.734
None of us do, and then we,

00:18:35.734 --> 00:18:37.297
you know, have our break and we win.

00:18:37.297 --> 00:18:39.441
And you can do it as well.

00:18:39.441 --> 00:18:42.460
Most people only pay
attention to the final product

00:18:42.460 --> 00:18:44.877
of a successful entrepreneur.

00:18:47.487 --> 00:18:48.889
They say things like,

00:18:48.889 --> 00:18:50.625
"I can never be like them."

00:18:50.625 --> 00:18:52.292
or "They got lucky."

00:18:54.130 --> 00:18:56.742
What most don't see is
what they've overcome.

